EXT. SALT FLAT - DAWN

A blinding plain of cracked white earth under a pink sky. Heat shimmer does not yet rise. A single abandoned jeep, windshield spiderwebbed, sits sunk to its axles. Beside it, a tarp stretched on poles makes a shelter no bigger than a closet.

Under the tarp, DR. CORDELIA ADEBAYO-FROST (40s, geologist, sunhat, parched lips) rations water into four tin cups with the fierce concentration of a priest. Next to her, her field assistant DESMOND "DEZ" MAKINDE (20s, bandaged ankle) leans against the jeep's tire, eyes closed.

Further off, a STRANGER sits cross-legged on the salt, facing away, a battered canvas pack beside him. He has been there since midnight. He has not spoken.

Standing watch at the tarp's edge, TAVITA LEOTA (50s, the driver, wide-shouldered, a rag knotted over his head) scans the horizon through binoculars.

CORDELIA
Dez, drink.

DEZ
Save it.

CORDELIA
Drink.

He opens his eyes, takes the cup, swallows. She watches the cup, not the man.

TAVITA
Nothing moving.

CORDELIA
There never is, until there is.

TAVITA
(lowering the binoculars)
I do not like that one.

CORDELIA
Who?

TAVITA
The man.

He nods toward the Stranger. Cordelia looks. The Stranger has not moved.

CORDELIA
He sat down and has not asked for anything.

TAVITA
That is what worries me.

DEZ
Maybe he's just tired.

TAVITA
Tired men ask for water.

Cordelia rises, takes a fourth cup, crosses the salt. The crust crunches. She stops a few paces behind the Stranger.

CORDELIA
You are welcome to this.

STRANGER
(without turning)
Thank you, Doctor.

CORDELIA
You know who I am.

STRANGER
I know you came looking for the old brine lake. I came for the same reason.

He rises, brushes salt from his knees, turns. Gaunt, sunburnt, mid-fifties, eyes the color of weak tea. He takes the cup but doesn't drink.

CORDELIA
And you are?

STRANGER
Matthias.

CORDELIA
Matthias what?

MATTHIAS
Matthias is enough.

TAVITA
(calling)
Doctor! Step back from him.

Cordelia does not move. Dez struggles upright. Matthias glances at Tavita, at Dez, and then at the sky, where a thin line of dust has begun to climb the horizon.

MATTHIAS
You should drink that yourselves. A truck is coming.

TAVITA
Whose truck?

MATTHIAS
Mine.

A beat. Everyone looks at the dust.

DEZ
(whispering)
He was waiting for rescue the whole time?

CORDELIA
No. He was waiting for us.

Tavita raises his binoculars, then drops them, and takes a step backward. Dez grabs the jeep's hood. Cordelia, calm, sets her cup on the salt. All four stand frozen under the pink sky as the engine's drone grows.

MATTHIAS
Don't be afraid. I only want what you are looking for.

CORDELIA
And if we say no?

MATTHIAS
Then you may walk home.
